# Pinned versions for CI's floating external dependencies.
#
# These are fetched fresh (or cache-restored) on every workflow run rather
# than vendored, so an unpinned `ref: master` means CI silently rides
# whatever upstream shipped that day -- including a change that breaks a
# test here with no corresponding change on our side. Pin to a tagged
# release and bump deliberately (by hand, after checking upstream's
# changelog/release notes) rather than drifting automatically.
#
# CEdev itself and convbin are already pinned via a release tarball URL /
# git ref respectively at their own call sites; they don't need an entry
# here, but should follow the same "bump deliberately" discipline.
#
# Usage in a workflow step:
#   CEMU_REF=$(grep '^CEMU_REF=' .github/ci-versions.env | cut -d= -f2)
# or source the whole file:
#   set -a; source .github/ci-versions.env; set +a

# No tagged CEmu release has autotester saveVar support (tests.yml depends
# on it, see "Verify saveVar Support In Autotester") -- it only ever landed
# on master (commit 91b32f47, 2024-12-04, "autotester: add saveVar
# command"), so pin to that exact commit rather than riding master's
# ongoing changes, which is also what we want anyway after a crash that
# only reproduced against master-at-some-later-point, not locally.
# https://github.com/CE-Programming/CEmu/commit/91b32f47b9608aeb55689e85267f780d6c4d58e6
CEMU_REF=91b32f47b9608aeb55689e85267f780d6c4d58e6

# https://github.com/CE-Programming/toolchain/releases
TOOLCHAIN_REF=v15.0
